//@version=6
// ==============================================================================================
//                        B U L L   &   B E A R S   V O L U M E
// ==============================================================================================
//
//  Indicator Name : Bull & Bears Volume
//  Author         : Forex_Market_Insights
//  Version        : v6.1 - July 2026
//  Pine Version   : Pine Script v6
//  Script Type    : Separate pane dashboard
//
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  A U T H O R   V E R I F I C A T I O N   D E C L A R A T I O N
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  I am Forex_Market_Insights, the publisher and sole original author of this exact
//  implementation of "Bull & Bears Volume." I designed the architecture of this tool, wrote every
//  line of the Pine Script v6 code contained in this file, tested it across multiple asset classes
//  and timeframes, and I take full and sole ownership and responsibility for it.
//
//  Specifically, I independently designed and coded: the close-position volume split that divides
//  each bar's activity into estimated buying and selling; the dual data-source architecture that
//  lets the dashboard read either the chart's own symbol across several timeframes or a watchlist
//  of separate instruments; the multi-timeframe request layer with its automatic suppression of
//  timeframes below the chart's own; the multi-symbol request layer with graceful handling of
//  blank and unresolvable entries; the per-instrument normalisation that scales every pair of bars
//  to its own dominance ratio so that markets of wildly different volume magnitudes remain
//  directly comparable; the dashboard geometry engine that lays out the frame, the title band, the
//  baseline, the paired bars and every label from the entry count and the configured spacing; the
//  sorting engine with its three ordering modes; the aggregate bias reading; the missing-data
//  handling that keeps the layout intact when a source returns nothing; the value formatter; and
//  the alert framework.
//
//  This declaration is made for this specific version of the script (v6.1, July 2026). Any future
//  modified version I publish will carry its own updated declaration in this same header.
//
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  O R I G I N A L   I N D I C A T O R   S C R I P T   I M P L E M E N T A T I O N
//  V E R I F I C A T I O N   A N D   D E C L A R A T I O N
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  I verify and declare that this script is an original implementation authored from scratch by
//  Forex_Market_Insights. No portion of this code was copied, ported, decompiled, translated,
//  reverse-engineered or adapted from any other author's closed-source, invite-only, protected or
//  open-source script. No third-party library and no republished open-source script forms any part
//  of this work, and no other author's dashboard layout or code was reproduced.
//
//  I acknowledge openly that the underlying concept is public and widely taught: splitting a bar's
//  volume into estimated buying and selling according to where that bar closed within its own
//  range, and comparing several data sources side by side to read broad sentiment. These ideas
//  belong to no single author. The close-position split in particular is a long established
//  estimation technique found in countless public tools and textbooks.
//
//  I also acknowledge, and state again in the honest disclosure below, that this split is an
//  approximation derived from candle geometry. It is not order book data and it is not real
//  aggressor-side classification. No script built on standard open, high, low, close and volume
//  can produce genuine order flow, and I make no such claim.
//
//  My original contribution, and what this declaration covers, is the specific code
//  implementation: my own dual-source architecture, my own multi-timeframe request structure and
//  its lower-timeframe guard, my own per-instrument dominance normalisation, my own layout
//  geometry engine, my own sorting model, my own aggregate bias reading, my own missing-data
//  handling and my own presentation layer. Conceptual overlap with other volume dashboards is
//  therefore unavoidable and expected, but there is no source-code overlap of any kind.
//
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  W H A T   T H I S   I N D I C A T O R   D O E S
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  Bull & Bears Volume answers one question: right now, across the data I care about, is activity
//  flowing into buying or into selling.
//
//  1) THE VOLUME SPLIT
//     For every bar, total volume is divided into an estimated buying portion and an estimated
//     selling portion according to where that bar closed inside its own range. A bar closing near
//     its high is credited mostly to buyers, one closing near its low mostly to sellers, and one
//     closing mid-range splits close to evenly.
//
//  2) TWO DATA SOURCES, SELECTABLE
//
//     CHART SYMBOL ACROSS TIMEFRAMES, the default. The dashboard reads whatever instrument the
//     chart is showing and displays its buying versus selling on several timeframes at once. Apply
//     it to gold and it shows gold. Apply it to Ethereum and it shows Ethereum. Nothing needs
//     configuring, nothing can be an invalid symbol, and it works on every market immediately.
//     Reading one instrument across the hourly, four-hourly, daily and weekly at the same time
//     tells you whether short-term flow agrees with the larger picture or is fighting it.
//
//     SYMBOL WATCHLIST. The dashboard reads up to twenty separate instruments side by side on one
//     timeframe. This is the market-wide sentiment view: point it at twenty crypto pairs, or
//     twenty currency pairs, or a mixed basket, and read the whole group at a glance. Any slot
//     left blank falls back to the chart's own symbol, and any entry that cannot be resolved is
//     reported as unavailable rather than breaking the script.
//
//  3) PER-SOURCE NORMALISATION, AND WHY IT MATTERS
//     This is the single most important design decision in the tool. Each pair of bars is scaled
//     to its own buying-versus-selling ratio rather than to a shared absolute scale. Bitcoin might
//     trade billions while a small altcoin trades thousands; on a shared scale the small one would
//     be an invisible sliver and the dashboard would be useless. Normalised per source, every pair
//     reads as a clean dominance percentage, so a source with seventy percent buying looks
//     identical whether it traded a billion or a thousand. The raw figures are still printed above
//     each bar for anyone who wants the absolute numbers.
//
//  4) AGGREGATE BIAS
//     Because every source is reduced to a comparable dominance figure, they can be summed. The
//     title band reports how many sources are currently buy-dominant and gives a single overall
//     bias reading.
//
//  5) SORTING
//     Sources can be shown in the order entered, sorted by strongest buying, or sorted by
//     strongest selling, which puts whatever you are hunting for at the left edge.
//
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  H O N E S T   D I S C L O S U R E   O N   M E T H O D
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  I state the following plainly so nothing here is oversold.
//
//  The buy and sell split is an ESTIMATE derived from where each bar closed within its own range.
//  It is not order book data, it is not real bid and ask classification, and it cannot see which
//  side was the aggressor on any individual trade. A bar closing on its high is credited to buyers
//  by this method even if that high was reached on a single small print. No indicator built on
//  standard open, high, low, close and volume can do better, and any tool claiming to show genuine
//  order flow from those five inputs is overstating what it has.
//
//  Read this dashboard as a directional bias comparison, not as precise flow figures.
//
//  A second point of honesty: the tool depends on the data source publishing real volume. Crypto
//  exchange pairs, futures and equities do. A great many spot Forex, CFD and metals feeds publish
//  none at all, and those sources will simply show as having no volume. That is a data limitation,
//  not a fault in the script, and the dashboard marks such entries clearly rather than inventing
//  numbers for them.
//
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  W H Y   T H I S   R U N S   I N   I T S   O W N   P A N E
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  A dashboard of this size drawn onto the price chart has to be positioned in price coordinates,
//  which forces the chart to rescale and crushes the candles into a thin strip at the top. The
//  dashboard becomes readable at the cost of making the chart useless.
//
//  This implementation runs in its own pane on a clean zero to one hundred percentage scale. The
//  dashboard is identical, the price chart above it is untouched, and the vertical axis now means
//  something: it is the dominance percentage.
//
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  L I V E   B E H A V I O U R   A N D   R E P A I N T I N G   S T A T E M E N T
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  The dashboard renders on the most recent bar and refreshes live as new data arrives, which is
//  the entire purpose of a real-time dashboard. It holds no historical drawings, so there is no
//  history for it to repaint.
//
//  All external requests use lookahead off, so no future data from any source can reach a past
//  bar. When a requested timeframe is higher than the chart timeframe, the figures shown are those
//  of the currently forming higher-timeframe bar and will keep moving until that bar closes. That
//  is correct live behaviour and is stated here so it is not mistaken for anything else.
//
//  Timeframes lower than the chart's own cannot be requested reliably from a higher-timeframe
//  chart, so the script detects and skips them and marks them as unavailable rather than showing
//  a misleading figure.
//
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  D I S C L A I M E R
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  This tool is for educational and informational purposes only. It does not constitute financial
//  advice. Trading involves risk; past patterns do not guarantee future results. The buy and sell
//  figures are estimates derived from candle geometry, not real order flow. Use proper risk
//  management and consult a licensed financial advisor before trading real capital.
// ==============================================================================================

indicator("Bull & Bears Volume", "B&B Volume", overlay = false, max_boxes_count = 500, max_lines_count = 100, max_labels_count = 500)

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  I N P U T S
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
gGen = "=====  DATA SOURCE  ====="
dataMode = input.string("Chart Symbol Across Timeframes", "Mode", options = ["Chart Symbol Across Timeframes", "Symbol Watchlist"], group = gGen, tooltip = "Chart Symbol Across Timeframes reads whatever instrument the chart is showing, on several timeframes at once. It works on every market with no configuration.\n\nSymbol Watchlist reads up to twenty separate instruments side by side on one timeframe.")
sortMode = input.string("As Entered", "Order", options = ["As Entered", "Strongest Buying First", "Strongest Selling First"], group = gGen)
title    = input.string("Bull & Bears Volume", "Dashboard Title", group = gGen)

gTf = "=====  TIMEFRAMES  (chart symbol mode)  ====="
tfOn1 = input.bool(true, "", group = gTf, inline = "f1")
tfS1  = input.timeframe("5",   "", group = gTf, inline = "f1")
tfOn2 = input.bool(true, "", group = gTf, inline = "f2")
tfS2  = input.timeframe("15",  "", group = gTf, inline = "f2")
tfOn3 = input.bool(true, "", group = gTf, inline = "f3")
tfS3  = input.timeframe("60",  "", group = gTf, inline = "f3")
tfOn4 = input.bool(true, "", group = gTf, inline = "f4")
tfS4  = input.timeframe("240", "", group = gTf, inline = "f4")
tfOn5 = input.bool(true, "", group = gTf, inline = "f5")
tfS5  = input.timeframe("1D",  "", group = gTf, inline = "f5")
tfOn6 = input.bool(true, "", group = gTf, inline = "f6")
tfS6  = input.timeframe("1W",  "", group = gTf, inline = "f6")
tfOn7 = input.bool(true, "", group = gTf, inline = "f7")
tfS7  = input.timeframe("1M",  "", group = gTf, inline = "f7")
tfOn8 = input.bool(false, "", group = gTf, inline = "f8")
tfS8  = input.timeframe("3M",  "", group = gTf, inline = "f8")

gWl = "=====  WATCHLIST TIMEFRAME  ====="
wlTf = input.timeframe("", "Watchlist Timeframe", group = gWl, tooltip = "Leave empty to follow the chart timeframe. Set it to 1D for a daily sentiment read across the whole watchlist.")

gLay = "=====  LAYOUT  ====="
slotW    = input.int(9, "Slot Width (bars per entry)", minval = 4, maxval = 40, group = gLay)
barW     = input.int(3, "Bar Width (bars)", minval = 1, maxval = 12, group = gLay)
rightPad = input.int(3, "Right Offset (bars)", minval = 0, maxval = 60, group = gLay)
showVals = input.bool(true, "Show Volume Values", group = gLay)
showName = input.bool(true, "Show Source Names", group = gLay)
showPx   = input.bool(true, "Show Prices", group = gLay)
showPct  = input.bool(true, "Show Dominance Percent", group = gLay)
txtSize  = input.string("Tiny", "Text Size", options = ["Tiny", "Small", "Normal"], group = gLay)

gSty = "=====  STYLE  ====="
colBuy   = input.color(#26c281, "Buying",  group = gSty, inline = "a")
colSell  = input.color(#e05c5c, "Selling", group = gSty, inline = "a")
colFrame = input.color(#a48ce0, "Frame",   group = gSty, inline = "b")
colTitle = input.color(color.white, "Title Text", group = gSty, inline = "b")
colValB  = input.color(#26c281, "Buy Value Text",  group = gSty, inline = "c")
colValS  = input.color(#e8b339, "Sell Value Text", group = gSty, inline = "c")
colPxUp  = input.color(#26c281, "Price Up",   group = gSty, inline = "d")
colPxDn  = input.color(#ff5c8a, "Price Down", group = gSty, inline = "d")
colName  = input.color(#b2b5be, "Source Name", group = gSty)
barTrans = input.int(25, "Bar Transparency", minval = 0, maxval = 100, group = gSty)

// Symbols are plain text fields on purpose. The symbol picker widget validates its contents and
// raises "Invalid symbol" for any entry it cannot resolve, even for slots that are switched off.
// A text field never does that, and unresolvable entries are handled at runtime instead.
gS1 = "=====  WATCHLIST 1 - 10   (blank = chart symbol)  ====="
on01 = input.bool(true,  "", group = gS1, inline = "01")
sy01 = input.string("",  "", group = gS1, inline = "01")
on02 = input.bool(false, "", group = gS1, inline = "02")
sy02 = input.string("",  "", group = gS1, inline = "02")
on03 = input.bool(false, "", group = gS1, inline = "03")
sy03 = input.string("",  "", group = gS1, inline = "03")
on04 = input.bool(false, "", group = gS1, inline = "04")
sy04 = input.string("",  "", group = gS1, inline = "04")
on05 = input.bool(false, "", group = gS1, inline = "05")
sy05 = input.string("",  "", group = gS1, inline = "05")
on06 = input.bool(false, "", group = gS1, inline = "06")
sy06 = input.string("",  "", group = gS1, inline = "06")
on07 = input.bool(false, "", group = gS1, inline = "07")
sy07 = input.string("",  "", group = gS1, inline = "07")
on08 = input.bool(false, "", group = gS1, inline = "08")
sy08 = input.string("",  "", group = gS1, inline = "08")
on09 = input.bool(false, "", group = gS1, inline = "09")
sy09 = input.string("",  "", group = gS1, inline = "09")
on10 = input.bool(false, "", group = gS1, inline = "10")
sy10 = input.string("",  "", group = gS1, inline = "10")

gS2 = "=====  WATCHLIST 11 - 20   (blank = chart symbol)  ====="
on11 = input.bool(false, "", group = gS2, inline = "11")
sy11 = input.string("",  "", group = gS2, inline = "11")
on12 = input.bool(false, "", group = gS2, inline = "12")
sy12 = input.string("",  "", group = gS2, inline = "12")
on13 = input.bool(false, "", group = gS2, inline = "13")
sy13 = input.string("",  "", group = gS2, inline = "13")
on14 = input.bool(false, "", group = gS2, inline = "14")
sy14 = input.string("",  "", group = gS2, inline = "14")
on15 = input.bool(false, "", group = gS2, inline = "15")
sy15 = input.string("",  "", group = gS2, inline = "15")
on16 = input.bool(false, "", group = gS2, inline = "16")
sy16 = input.string("",  "", group = gS2, inline = "16")
on17 = input.bool(false, "", group = gS2, inline = "17")
sy17 = input.string("",  "", group = gS2, inline = "17")
on18 = input.bool(false, "", group = gS2, inline = "18")
sy18 = input.string("",  "", group = gS2, inline = "18")
on19 = input.bool(false, "", group = gS2, inline = "19")
sy19 = input.string("",  "", group = gS2, inline = "19")
on20 = input.bool(false, "", group = gS2, inline = "20")
sy20 = input.string("",  "", group = gS2, inline = "20")

string szT = txtSize == "Small" ? size.small : txtSize == "Normal" ? size.normal : size.tiny
bool   tfMode = dataMode == "Chart Symbol Across Timeframes"

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  T H E   V O L U M E   S P L I T
//  Each bar's volume is divided by where that bar closed inside its own range. This is an
//  estimate derived from candle geometry, not order book data. See the disclosure in the header.
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
volSplit() =>
    float rng = high - low
    float v   = nz(volume)
    float bv  = rng > 0 ? v * (close - low) / rng : v * 0.5
    float sv  = rng > 0 ? v * (high - close) / rng : v * 0.5
    [bv, sv, close, open]

// blank entry falls back to the chart's own symbol, so no slot can ever be invalid
resolveSym(string s) =>
    str.length(str.replace_all(s, " ", "")) == 0 ? syminfo.tickerid : s

grabSym(string sym) =>
    request.security(resolveSym(sym), wlTf, volSplit(), gaps = barmerge.gaps_off, lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_off, ignore_invalid_symbol = true)

grabTf(string t) =>
    request.security(syminfo.tickerid, t, volSplit(), gaps = barmerge.gaps_off, lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_off, ignore_invalid_symbol = true)

// a timeframe below the chart's own cannot be requested reliably, so it is skipped and reported
tfUsable(string t) =>
    int a = timeframe.in_seconds(t)
    int b = timeframe.in_seconds(timeframe.period)
    not na(a) and not na(b) and a >= b

// ---- chart symbol across timeframes ----
[tb1, ts1, tc1, to1] = grabTf(tfS1)
[tb2, ts2, tc2, to2] = grabTf(tfS2)
[tb3, ts3, tc3, to3] = grabTf(tfS3)
[tb4, ts4, tc4, to4] = grabTf(tfS4)
[tb5, ts5, tc5, to5] = grabTf(tfS5)
[tb6, ts6, tc6, to6] = grabTf(tfS6)
[tb7, ts7, tc7, to7] = grabTf(tfS7)
[tb8, ts8, tc8, to8] = grabTf(tfS8)

// ---- watchlist ----
[b01, s01, c01, o01] = grabSym(sy01)
[b02, s02, c02, o02] = grabSym(sy02)
[b03, s03, c03, o03] = grabSym(sy03)
[b04, s04, c04, o04] = grabSym(sy04)
[b05, s05, c05, o05] = grabSym(sy05)
[b06, s06, c06, o06] = grabSym(sy06)
[b07, s07, c07, o07] = grabSym(sy07)
[b08, s08, c08, o08] = grabSym(sy08)
[b09, s09, c09, o09] = grabSym(sy09)
[b10, s10, c10, o10] = grabSym(sy10)
[b11, s11, c11, o11] = grabSym(sy11)
[b12, s12, c12, o12] = grabSym(sy12)
[b13, s13, c13, o13] = grabSym(sy13)
[b14, s14, c14, o14] = grabSym(sy14)
[b15, s15, c15, o15] = grabSym(sy15)
[b16, s16, c16, o16] = grabSym(sy16)
[b17, s17, c17, o17] = grabSym(sy17)
[b18, s18, c18, o18] = grabSym(sy18)
[b19, s19, c19, o19] = grabSym(sy19)
[b20, s20, c20, o20] = grabSym(sy20)

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  H E L P E R S
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
fmtVal(float v) =>
    string s = "n/a"
    if not na(v) and v > 0
        float a = math.abs(v)
        s := a >= 1e12 ? str.tostring(v / 1e12, "#.##") + "T" : a >= 1e9 ? str.tostring(v / 1e9, "#.##") + "B" : a >= 1e6 ? str.tostring(v / 1e6, "#.###") + "M" : a >= 1e3 ? str.tostring(v / 1e3, "#.###") + "K" : str.tostring(v, "#.##")
    s

fmtPx(float p) =>
    string s = "-"
    if not na(p)
        s := p >= 1000 ? str.tostring(p, "#.##") : p >= 1 ? str.tostring(p, "#.####") : str.tostring(p, "#.########")
    s

shortName(string s) =>
    string t = resolveSym(s)
    int cut = str.pos(t, ":")
    if not na(cut)
        t := str.substring(t, cut + 1)
    t

prettyTf(string t) =>
    int sec = timeframe.in_seconds(t)
    string r = t
    if not na(sec)
        r := sec < 60 ? str.tostring(sec) + "s" : sec < 3600 ? str.tostring(sec / 60) + "m" : sec < 86400 ? str.tostring(sec / 3600) + "H" : sec < 604800 ? str.tostring(sec / 86400) + "D" : sec < 2592000 ? str.tostring(sec / 604800) + "W" : str.tostring(math.round(sec / 2592000)) + "M"
    r

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  A S S E M B L E   T H E   D A T A   S E T
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
var array<string> names = array.new<string>()
var array<float>  buys  = array.new<float>()
var array<float>  sells = array.new<float>()
var array<float>  pxs   = array.new<float>()
var array<float>  opns  = array.new<float>()
var array<bool>   avail = array.new<bool>()

addRow(bool on, string nm, float b, float s, float c, float o, bool ok) =>
    if on
        names.push(nm)
        buys.push(nz(b))
        sells.push(nz(s))
        pxs.push(c)
        opns.push(o)
        avail.push(ok)

int   bullCount = 0
int   liveCount = 0
float biasSum   = 0.0

if barstate.islast
    names.clear()
    buys.clear()
    sells.clear()
    pxs.clear()
    opns.clear()
    avail.clear()

    if tfMode
        addRow(tfOn1, prettyTf(tfS1), tb1, ts1, tc1, to1, tfUsable(tfS1))
        addRow(tfOn2, prettyTf(tfS2), tb2, ts2, tc2, to2, tfUsable(tfS2))
        addRow(tfOn3, prettyTf(tfS3), tb3, ts3, tc3, to3, tfUsable(tfS3))
        addRow(tfOn4, prettyTf(tfS4), tb4, ts4, tc4, to4, tfUsable(tfS4))
        addRow(tfOn5, prettyTf(tfS5), tb5, ts5, tc5, to5, tfUsable(tfS5))
        addRow(tfOn6, prettyTf(tfS6), tb6, ts6, tc6, to6, tfUsable(tfS6))
        addRow(tfOn7, prettyTf(tfS7), tb7, ts7, tc7, to7, tfUsable(tfS7))
        addRow(tfOn8, prettyTf(tfS8), tb8, ts8, tc8, to8, tfUsable(tfS8))
    else
        addRow(on01, shortName(sy01), b01, s01, c01, o01, true)
        addRow(on02, shortName(sy02), b02, s02, c02, o02, true)
        addRow(on03, shortName(sy03), b03, s03, c03, o03, true)
        addRow(on04, shortName(sy04), b04, s04, c04, o04, true)
        addRow(on05, shortName(sy05), b05, s05, c05, o05, true)
        addRow(on06, shortName(sy06), b06, s06, c06, o06, true)
        addRow(on07, shortName(sy07), b07, s07, c07, o07, true)
        addRow(on08, shortName(sy08), b08, s08, c08, o08, true)
        addRow(on09, shortName(sy09), b09, s09, c09, o09, true)
        addRow(on10, shortName(sy10), b10, s10, c10, o10, true)
        addRow(on11, shortName(sy11), b11, s11, c11, o11, true)
        addRow(on12, shortName(sy12), b12, s12, c12, o12, true)
        addRow(on13, shortName(sy13), b13, s13, c13, o13, true)
        addRow(on14, shortName(sy14), b14, s14, c14, o14, true)
        addRow(on15, shortName(sy15), b15, s15, c15, o15, true)
        addRow(on16, shortName(sy16), b16, s16, c16, o16, true)
        addRow(on17, shortName(sy17), b17, s17, c17, o17, true)
        addRow(on18, shortName(sy18), b18, s18, c18, o18, true)
        addRow(on19, shortName(sy19), b19, s19, c19, o19, true)
        addRow(on20, shortName(sy20), b20, s20, c20, o20, true)

    // ---- sorting ----
    int n = names.size()
    if sortMode != "As Entered" and n > 1
        for i = 0 to n - 2
            for j = 0 to n - 2 - i
                float ta = buys.get(j) + sells.get(j)
                float tb = buys.get(j + 1) + sells.get(j + 1)
                float da = ta > 0 ? buys.get(j) / ta : 0.5
                float db = tb > 0 ? buys.get(j + 1) / tb : 0.5
                bool swap = sortMode == "Strongest Buying First" ? db > da : db < da
                if swap
                    string tn = names.get(j)
                    float  t1 = buys.get(j)
                    float  t2 = sells.get(j)
                    float  t3 = pxs.get(j)
                    float  t4 = opns.get(j)
                    bool   t5 = avail.get(j)
                    names.set(j, names.get(j + 1))
                    buys.set(j, buys.get(j + 1))
                    sells.set(j, sells.get(j + 1))
                    pxs.set(j, pxs.get(j + 1))
                    opns.set(j, opns.get(j + 1))
                    avail.set(j, avail.get(j + 1))
                    names.set(j + 1, tn)
                    buys.set(j + 1, t1)
                    sells.set(j + 1, t2)
                    pxs.set(j + 1, t3)
                    opns.set(j + 1, t4)
                    avail.set(j + 1, t5)

    // ---- aggregate bias ----
    if n > 0
        for i = 0 to n - 1
            float tot = buys.get(i) + sells.get(i)
            if tot > 0 and avail.get(i)
                liveCount += 1
                float dom = buys.get(i) / tot
                biasSum += dom
                if dom > 0.5
                    bullCount += 1

float  biasAvg = liveCount > 0 ? biasSum / liveCount * 100.0 : na
string biasTxt = na(biasAvg) ? "NO DATA" : biasAvg >= 60 ? "STRONG BUYING" : biasAvg >= 53 ? "BUYING" : biasAvg > 47 ? "BALANCED" : biasAvg > 40 ? "SELLING" : "STRONG SELLING"

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  D A S H B O A R D   R E N D E R I N G
//  The pane scale is a clean 0 to 100 dominance percentage. Every bar pair is normalised to its
//  own source, which is what keeps a thousand-dollar market and a billion-dollar market directly
//  comparable inside the same frame.
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
var array<box>   dBox = array.new<box>()
var array<label> dLbl = array.new<label>()
var array<line>  dLin = array.new<line>()

wipe() =>
    if dBox.size() > 0
        for b in dBox
            box.delete(b)
        dBox.clear()
    if dLbl.size() > 0
        for l in dLbl
            label.delete(l)
        dLbl.clear()
    if dLin.size() > 0
        for l in dLin
            line.delete(l)
        dLin.clear()

if barstate.islast
    wipe()

    int n = names.size()
    if n > 0
        int   rightX = bar_index + rightPad
        int   width  = n * slotW + 4
        int   leftX  = rightX - width
        float topY   = 132.0
        float titleY = 112.0
        float baseY  = 0.0
        float botY   = -34.0

        dBox.push(box.new(leftX, topY, rightX, botY, xloc = xloc.bar_index, border_color = colFrame, border_width = 3, bgcolor = color.new(colFrame, 96)))
        dBox.push(box.new(leftX, topY, rightX, titleY, xloc = xloc.bar_index, border_color = color.new(colFrame, 100), bgcolor = color.new(colFrame, 15)))

        string src  = tfMode ? syminfo.ticker + " across timeframes" : "watchlist"
        string head = title + "   |   " + src + "   |   " + (na(biasAvg) ? "no volume data on this feed" : str.tostring(biasAvg, "#.#") + "%  " + biasTxt + "   |   " + str.tostring(bullCount) + " of " + str.tostring(liveCount) + " buy-dominant")
        dLbl.push(label.new(math.round((leftX + rightX) / 2), (topY + titleY) / 2, head, xloc = xloc.bar_index, style = label.style_none, textcolor = colTitle, size = szT))

        dLin.push(line.new(leftX + 1, baseY, rightX - 1, baseY, xloc = xloc.bar_index, color = color.new(colFrame, 55), style = line.style_dotted, width = 1))
        dLin.push(line.new(leftX + 1, 50.0, rightX - 1, 50.0, xloc = xloc.bar_index, color = color.new(colFrame, 80), style = line.style_dotted, width = 1))

        for i = 0 to n - 1
            float bv   = buys.get(i)
            float sv   = sells.get(i)
            float tot  = bv + sv
            bool  ok   = avail.get(i)
            bool  live = tot > 0 and ok

            float bh = live ? bv / tot * 100.0 : 0.0
            float sh = live ? sv / tot * 100.0 : 0.0

            int slot = leftX + 2 + i * slotW
            int gx1  = slot
            int gx2  = slot + barW
            int rx1  = gx2 + 1
            int rx2  = rx1 + barW

            if live
                dBox.push(box.new(gx1, bh, gx2, baseY, xloc = xloc.bar_index, border_color = color.new(colBuy, 20), border_width = 1, bgcolor = color.new(colBuy, barTrans)))
                dBox.push(box.new(rx1, sh, rx2, baseY, xloc = xloc.bar_index, border_color = color.new(colSell, 20), border_width = 1, bgcolor = color.new(colSell, barTrans)))

                if showVals
                    dLbl.push(label.new(math.round((gx1 + gx2) / 2), bh + 3, fmtVal(bv), xloc = xloc.bar_index, style = label.style_none, textcolor = colValB, size = szT))
                    dLbl.push(label.new(math.round((rx1 + rx2) / 2), sh + 3, fmtVal(sv), xloc = xloc.bar_index, style = label.style_none, textcolor = colValS, size = szT))
                if showPct
                    dLbl.push(label.new(math.round((gx1 + rx2) / 2), -6.0, str.tostring(bh, "#") + " / " + str.tostring(sh, "#"), xloc = xloc.bar_index, style = label.style_none, textcolor = bh >= sh ? colBuy : colSell, size = szT))
            else
                dLbl.push(label.new(math.round((gx1 + rx2) / 2), 8.0, ok ? "no\nvolume" : "below\nchart TF", xloc = xloc.bar_index, style = label.style_none, textcolor = color.new(colName, 25), size = szT))

            if showName
                dLbl.push(label.new(math.round((gx1 + rx2) / 2), -16.0, names.get(i), xloc = xloc.bar_index, style = label.style_none, textcolor = colName, size = szT))
            if showPx
                float px = pxs.get(i)
                float op = opns.get(i)
                color pc = na(px) or na(op) ? colName : px >= op ? colPxUp : colPxDn
                dLbl.push(label.new(math.round((gx1 + rx2) / 2), -26.0, fmtPx(px), xloc = xloc.bar_index, style = label.style_none, textcolor = pc, size = szT))

plot(0.0,   "Scale Floor",   color = color.new(color.gray, 100), display = display.none)
plot(100.0, "Scale Ceiling", color = color.new(color.gray, 100), display = display.none)

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  A L E R T S
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
alertcondition(not na(biasAvg) and biasAvg >= 60 and nz(biasAvg[1], 50) < 60, "B&B - Turned Strongly Bullish", "Bull & Bears Volume: aggregate buying dominance moved above 60 percent.")
alertcondition(not na(biasAvg) and biasAvg <= 40 and nz(biasAvg[1], 50) > 40, "B&B - Turned Strongly Bearish", "Bull & Bears Volume: aggregate buying dominance fell below 40 percent.")
alertcondition(not na(biasAvg) and biasAvg > 50 and nz(biasAvg[1], 50) <= 50, "B&B - Bias Flipped Bullish", "Bull & Bears Volume: aggregate bias flipped to buying.")
alertcondition(not na(biasAvg) and biasAvg < 50 and nz(biasAvg[1], 50) >= 50, "B&B - Bias Flipped Bearish", "Bull & Bears Volume: aggregate bias flipped to selling.")

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  D A T A   W I N D O W   O U T P U T S
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
plot(biasAvg,   "Aggregate Buying Dominance %", color = color.new(color.orange, 100), display = display.data_window)
plot(bullCount, "Buy-Dominant Sources",         color = color.new(color.orange, 100), display = display.data_window)
plot(liveCount, "Sources With Volume",          color = color.new(color.orange, 100), display = display.data_window)